Janet-pkcs11 is a @link[https://janet-lang.org]{Janet} wrapper for PKCS #11 API.

## Source code

@p{@link[https://github.com/tttuuu888/janet-pkcs11]}

## Install

@codeblock```
[sudo] jpm install https://github.com/tttuuu888/janet-pkcs11.git
```

## Example

The following is an example of the process using Janet-pkcs11, including session opening, login, AES key generation, encryption, and decryption.  

In this example, libsofthsm2.so is used for module initialization, and it is assumed that a token labeled "test" has already been initialized and the user PIN is set to 123456.

The token can be initialized with softhsm2-util as follows:

@codeblock```
softhsm2-util --init-token --free --label test --so-pin 012345 --pin 123456
```

@codeblock[janet]```
(use pkcs11)

(def p11 (new "/usr/lib/softhsm/libsofthsm2.so"))

## find the slot holding the token labeled "test"
(def slot (find (fn [s] (= ((:get-token-info p11 s) :label) "test"))
                (:get-slot-list p11)))

(def session (:open-session p11 slot))

(:login session :user "123456")

(let [key (:generate-key session
                         {:mechanism     :CKM_AES_KEY_GEN}
                         {:CKA_KEY_TYPE  :CKK_AES
                          :CKA_VALUE_LEN 32
                          :CKA_ENCRYPT   true
                          :CKA_DECRYPT   true})
      plain (hex-decode "000102030405060708090a0b0c0d0e0f")]

  ## encrypt
  (:encrypt-init session {:mechanism :CKM_AES_ECB} key)
  (def encrypted (:encrypt session plain))

  ## decrypt
  (:decrypt-init session {:mechanism :CKM_AES_ECB} key)
  (def decrypted (:decrypt session encrypted))

  ## check result
  (print "Plain:     " (hex-encode plain))
  (print "Decrypted: " (hex-encode decrypted)))

(:close session)
(:close p11)
```

More examples can be found in the test.
